      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T18:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the way that compat ioctl handlers are usually written.  Look at ext4_ioctl(), for example.  Usually most compat ioctls are either the same as the non-compat ioctls or just have different numbers, so it\u0027s simplest to handle them by calling the non-compat ioctl handler (after optionally translating the ioctl number).  It\u0027s not necessary to directly call the functions that implement each individual ioctl command.\n\nIn cases where a compat ioctl command actually has to be implemented differently, it can just be handled in the switch statement.  It happens that TIPC_IOC_SEND_MSG will need that, but that\u0027s the exception rather than the rule.",
      "parentUuid": "b193ace0_d2fce550",
